cartridge "SKY MAIL/AMY & CLAUDE/2026"

' SKY MAIL - an original game by Amy & Claude for Amy Studio, 2026, in Amy.
' You pilot the mail balloon over a village that wraps around (1024 px).
' The balloon only goes up (burner) or down (vent, or let it cool); it
' moves sideways only with the wind, and the wind is different at each
' height: 4 layers, each with its own direction and strength, shown by the
' cloud streaks drifting in that layer and by an arrow in column 2. Ride the
' layer that blows your way, then drop mail sacks onto the houses with a
' red flag (the sack keeps the balloon's drift and the winds it falls
' through bend its arc).
'
' Controls (either controller): LEFT button or stick UP = burner (heat:
' the balloon rises after a short delay), stick DOWN = vent (it sinks),
' nothing = the air cools to a slow sink; RIGHT button = drop a sack.
' Keypad not used.
' Rules (model.mjs is the same rules in JavaScript, checked in lockstep):
' - 5 sacks. Land on a tower top: fuel, and the bag is refilled (a sack
'   every 20 frames). Skim a hill: its parcel (+1 sack, +25), back 10 s later.
' - A sack on a flagged roof: 150 within 3 px of its middle, 100 within
'   8 px, else 50. Every flag done: the day is over (bonus 200 x day + fuel
'   / 30, +1 balloon up to 4), next day: more flags, stronger winds.
' - Lose a balloon: touching the ground, a spire, a rock or a tower's side,
'   lightning, or the sun setting (each day has 120 s, the sun crosses row
'   2). Roofs and hill sides only bump you up (and cost a little fuel).
'   Birds (a warning at the screen edge first) knock a sack off and push
'   you down. Thunderheads (from day 3) form grey, darken (rumble), then
'   push down whoever rides their layer and flash lightning (1.5 Hz).
' - Gusts: every 13-25 s one layer's wind changes; its arrow blinks between
'   the old and the new wind for 3 s first (2 Hz) with a whoosh.
'
' House frame: title (animated: the village scrolls, a balloon drifts,
' birds fly; a looping 30 s original tune, A A B A) with START / HOW TO
' PLAY / CREDITS; 3 HOW TO PLAY pages; game over: one press returns to the
' title. Nothing flashes over 3 Hz. At most 4 sprites on a line, no
' flicker: the balloon (3 sprites, at most 2 on a line), the sack, one bird
' a line (birds stay above y 96), popups (y 100-127), the parcel (y 140+).
'
' Screen: row 1 HUD (sacks, fuel, score, balloons, day), row 2 the sun,
' rows 3/7/11 cloud streaks of layers 0/1/2 (each drifts with its wind),
' rows 4-5/8-9/12-13 thunderheads, 15 far hills (camera / 2), 16-20 the
' village (camera), 21-23 road and fields (camera). Bands move by
' rewriting tile PATTERNS from pre-shifted ROM tables (the asm engine,
' SkBlit, in the vertical blank: sky bands on odd frames, village and road
' on even frames); names change only when the village crosses a cell.

